> > "At first spells act as expected" in spell.c with the same comment in
> > the current version.
>
> I didn't start compiling from source until the current version. Would you 
> mind telling me what actually was deleted? 

The comment originally read:

    /*
     * At first these act as expected.  As the character increases in
     * experience the spell increases in its ability.  Initially the
     * spells have their expected levels of damage.  When the hero level
     * reaches three times the level of the spell the spell does special
     * damage.  This special damage is indicated before each spell.  Note
     * even when the hero reaches three times the level of the spell she
     * still has the choice of casting either spell. Also the new level
     * of spell has an increased cost in casting it.
     */

> As it now stands, the quote reads thus:
> 
> 	/*
> 	 * At first spells act as expected.  As the hero increases in skill
> 	 * with the appropriate spell type, some spells increase in their
> 	 * effects, e.g. more damage, further distance, and so on, without
> 	 * additional cost to the spellcaster.
> 	 */

The msnner in which the comment was changed to match the code rather
than vice versa is what I find indicative of the DevTeam's intent.

> I would assume "increase in their effects" wouldn't mean "decrease in their 
> effects," at any rate.

Not every increase in an effect need be a _beneficial_ increase to the
player.

> (I also don't see why casting the spell while engulfed wouldn't harm
> the spellcaster regardless of level; after all, doesn't the ray
> explode on the nine squares on and surrounding the first monster it
> hits?)

That, I think, is an entirely separate issue: buzz() makes several
exceptions for ZT_SPELL(ZT_FIRE), but the if(u.uswallow) code isn't
one of them, and possibly should be. That's been the case since long
before skilled fireball was added to the game, however; fireballs
have exploded since 3.1.

